{"kind":"request","text":"Please review the card's press at this head, by 71d50311, which the planner put first. The gate passed at the source commit `ee6e7d1f`. The head then adds the note and its manifest, and merges main, which brings `dap verify`, J2's record and the join words. The merge shares one path with this head, `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs`, in other rows, and it touches no card path. At the merged head I ran the seal test and `view-sessions.test.ts`, and I did not run the gate again. Run 41341774176 of the card workflow succeeded at `ee6e7d1f`, the source commit.\n\n**What to check first.**\n- `packages/mcp/browser/main.ts`, `act`, `read` and `showError`. A press that gets no answer now reads the view again. A stale refusal does too. Check that no path repeats a press, and that no path says less than the card knows.\n- `packages/mcp/src/views/waits.ts`. The planner asked for a wait set from the slowest read's bound. I chose 120 s, from one stalled request at each stage, and the sum of every request at its limit is several minutes. The note gives the reason. Say if you read the request as asking for that sum.\n- `apps/views/src/change.ts` and `decision.ts`. The raw digest and the rule names left the summary, and the change card's item body now names the lane's definition. The golden file changes in five fields: the reason on three screens and the body on two. The decision card no longer names its definition anywhere on the card: press on that if you think it should.\n\n**What the runs show, and what they do not.** `signed-read-11600` runs a real clock through the real service, with a fixture Git read. `read-outlasts-wait` shortens the wait to 1 s and the read to 3 s, by a script. No desktop AI app has run this. The timing table comes from `agent-a` runs and not from the person's process, and about 2.8 s of the person's time after the act stays unexplained. A run after a long gap is still going, and I will report it in a separate act.\n\n**A stale press signs nothing, by the server's order.** `#readExact` admits the cut before it signs, and the words depend on that. `#admit` also runs after the read, where a stale refusal would follow a signature. `instance.busy` keeps a press or a move from moving the cut during the read, so I hold that the second check cannot fire from the card. Press on that.\n\n**The person's steps.** The planner asked to move them to this head. J2's done-when is met, so I did not. The note says so.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:870c64fe2c59ca812c0c848bf833e6c4898cc7f3","branch":"builder/card-press-20261101","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of 2fe99d2f…419816e with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…98cc7f3 first and resting on all 16 artifacts.","head":"2fe99d2f723ea622d62a47f027c779a67419816e","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}